{title: Christ, Whose Glory Fills the Skies}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Christ, whose [F]glory [C]fills the [G]skies
[Am]Christ, the [G]true, the [F]only [C]Light,
[C]Sun of [G]Righteous[F]ness, a[C]rise,
[C]Triumph [E]o'er the [Dm]shades of [Am]night;
[F]Dayspring [G]from on [F]high, be [E]near,
[Am]Daystar, [G]in my [F]heart a[C]ppear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Dark and [F]cheerless [C]is the [G]morn
[Am]Unac[G]compa[F]nied by [C]Thee;
[C]Joyless [G]is the [F]day's re[C]turn,
[C]Till Thy [E]mercy's [Dm]beams I [Am]see,
[F]Till Thou [G]inward [F]light im[E]part,
[Am]Glad my [G]eyes, and [F]warm my [C]heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Visit [F]then this [C]soul of [G]mine,
[Am]Pierce the [G]gloom of [F]sin and [C]grief;
[C]Fill me, [G]Radian[F]cy di[C]vine,
[C]Scatter [E]all my [Dm]unbe[Am]lief;
[F]More and [G]more Thy[F]self dis[E]play,
[Am]Shining [G]to the [F]perfect [C]day.
{end_of_verse}
